{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-server-ci-workflows-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-1","surface":"server","area":"server/ci-workflows","refs":["F-server-601","F-server-621","FN-A8-server-ci-workflows-1-07"],"severity":"S4","title":"The WhatsApp set-up and test runs always check the login_code message, even if sign-in is switched to another one","what":"The gym server lets MettleUp switch the WhatsApp sign-in message and its language to a different approved one with a setting. The set-up run that reports the message status and the test run that sends a sample both have the name login_code and English written in, and never read that setting. After a switch they would report on, and send, a message that sign-in no longer uses.","expected":"The set-up and test runs use the same message name and language as sign-in, or say clearly which one they checked and that sign-in may use another.","evidence":["deploy/panel/phoneCode.js:216","deploy/panel/wrangler.jsonc:64",".github/workflows/whatsapp-setup.yml:83-84",".github/workflows/whatsapp-probe.yml:53-57"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"probe-template-name-hard-coded","who":"MettleUp team","how_often":"only after the sign-in message is switched","fix_line":"Let both runs take the message name and language as an input, defaulting to what sign-in uses","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
